Am I the only one who's got a bit tired of Nethack? 

In the old days it was simple - go to the bottom, get the Amulet, come
back up. Great.

Then we started getting castles and so forth, which jazzed it up a bit.
Also nice.

Now, however, we have Quests. The Quests are good, but we're still stuck
with the long, boring trip to the bottom and a long, boring trip back up.
Perhaps it's time to consider condensing this part of the game? It made
sense before we had all these side trips; without the long trip you
wouldn't have had a game. Now, however, it's a dull interlude between the
fun bits.

This is how I see Nethack at present:
1) Building a character - this is different each time and is therefore fun.
2) Going on a Quest - there are a number of Quests, and they're not too long.
3) Going aaaaall the way down - you can do this pretty quickly.
4) Pissing about with hidden portals and stuff - done it once, done it a
hundred times.
5) Get the amulet, fight the wizard, fight the wizard, fight the wizard,
fight the wizard.... all this is the same every game, you're going through
levels you've already traversed, and it's *slow*.
6) Endgame.

I think that (5) could be a lot better were it to be compressed. Nethack
is now a sophisticated game. You don't need to make it difficult by being
slow; you can make it difficult by having clever levels and stuff - like
the Endgame.

How would I solve this? Easy. Let people teleport levels with the Amulet
so that they can skip the mazes and the dungeon once they've gone through
them once. If that makes the game too quick, just add a couple of fresh
levels in the endgame. The return upstairs is a serious drag. I have
several mega-powerful characters who have completed their Quest, but I
can't be stuffed returning with the Amulet. It's time to recognise that
Nethack has moved on.

